---
term: Social Charter
aka:
  - The Social Charter
section: intent
order: 10
definition: A system of social organization designed to advance society to better states more efficiently than traditional democratic or autocratic structures.
seeAlso:
  - question-of-arbitration
  - vanguard-interest
---
The Social Charter starts from two observations about existing political movements. Decentralized movements struggle to form and enact a clear agenda, which is the [[question of arbitration]]. Centralized movements are undermined by their leadership, which is the [[vanguard interest]].
